On Sat, 10 Oct 2026 09:54:54 -0700, Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com> wrote:
> I have a pretty simple notmuch tagging setup. The emacs notmuch saved
> searches config is pretty out of date at this point.

Yes. Most of the saved searches query new, unread, closed, and the
patch:* states, and nothing sets any of those now. The post-new hook
derives only inbox, sent and replied, and emacs adds draft.

> Simplify it, and
> provide useful saved searches based on my tags and usage patterns.

Posted as "[PATCH] emacs: Match notmuch saved searches to the list's
tags" [1]. Thirteen entries become five:

    i  inbox     tag:inbox
    p  patches   tag:inbox and subject:PATCH
    d  drafts    tag:draft
    s  sent      tag:sent
    a  all mail  *

"patches" is the review queue: series, and replies to them, that you
have not answered yet. "flagged" is gone because with flag sync off
it is local-only state, which the list decided against. The
:sort-order options are dropped too, since they only repeated the
newest-first default.

Two things are left for other patches. The "new" face in
notmuch-search-line-faces and notmuch-tag-formats is stale in the
same way. Say if you want it switched to inbox. The archive work in
"Archive messages that have the archive tag" [2] will set
notmuch-archive-tags and take archived mail out of inbox, and these
searches pick that up without any change.

